  "mechanism_narrative": "ACVR2B (constitutively active Ser/Thr kinase) transphosphorylates BMPR1A GS domain, activating SMAD1/5/8 signaling. Flexible_GS4 linker (~20 A) brings kinase domains into close proximity, mimicking natural BMP-induced heterotetramer assembly. Biased output is canonical BMP-SMAD signaling (ID1/2/3 targets) plus non-canonical TAK1-p38 and LIMK1 branches, with no RTK-like GRB2/SHC/RAS/MAPK adaptor recruitment because TGF-beta family receptors lack phosphotyrosine docking sites. ACVR2B is very lowly expressed in aged muscle (pc<=0.05), limiting target cell engagement.",
